chain_of_thought:
To expand the expression $(x+2)(3x-6)$, we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials). The distributive property states that $a(b+c) = ab + ac$.

Step 1: Distribute each term in the first binomial to each term in the second binomial.
\begin{align*}
(x+2)(3x-6) &= x(3x) + x(-6) + 2(3x) + 2(-6) \\
&= 3x^2 - 6x + 6x - 12
\end{align*}

Step 2: Combine like terms.
\begin{align*}
3x^2 - 6x + 6x - 12 &= 3x^2 - 12
\end{align*}

Therefore, the expanded form of $(x+2)(3x-6)$ is $\boxed{3x^2-12}$.

